Method and references
=====================

The controllers in this repository implement the artificial vector fields
described in the following works. The implementation was written from their
equations; equation numbers in the code and documentation refer to the thesis.

  A. M. C. Rezende, V. M. Gonçalves and L. C. A. Pimenta, "Constructive
  Time-Varying Vector Fields for Robot Navigation", IEEE Transactions on
  Robotics, vol. 38, no. 2, pp. 852-867, 2022.
  doi:10.1109/TRO.2021.3093674

  A. M. C. Rezende, "Vector field based guidance and control strategies for
  robot navigation", PhD thesis, Programa de Pós-Graduação em Engenharia
  Elétrica, Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais (UFMG), 2022.
  https://hdl.handle.net/1843/73611


Prior implementation (design inspiration only)
==============================================

vectorfield_stack (https://github.com/adrianomcr/vectorfield_stack) is the
ROS 1 implementation that accompanies the thesis. It is published without a
license and is registered at INPI (Instituto Nacional da Propriedade
Industrial, Brazil) under process BR512022000695-2, owned by Universidade
Federal de Minas Gerais (UFMG) and VALE S.A.

vectorfield_stack inspired the design of this project. No code from
vectorfield_stack is included in this repository, either verbatim or
translated.


